<Project>

  <!--
    backend/Directory.Build.props
    ============================================================================
    Shared MSBuild properties for the DnnMigration backend solution.

    MSBuild automatically imports this file into EVERY .csproj located anywhere
    beneath backend/, so these settings apply uniformly to all six projects:
      src/DnnMigration.Domain, src/DnnMigration.Application,
      src/DnnMigration.Infrastructure, src/DnnMigration.Api,
      tests/DnnMigration.UnitTests, tests/DnnMigration.IntegrationTests.

    Centralizing build configuration here keeps the individual .csproj files
    minimal; child projects do NOT restate these values.

    Structure reference (NOT a 1:1 port): the legacy VB.NET project
    Library/DotNetNuke.Library.vbproj enforced strictness via OptionExplicit On
    and OptionStrict On. Those map to the modern equivalents below: nullable
    reference types plus treat warnings as errors.

    Mandated build policy (AAP sections 0.7.1 / 0.7.2, NON-NEGOTIABLE):
      * net8.0 (.NET 8 LTS) target for all projects.
      * C# 12 language version.
      * Nullable reference types enabled.
      * Implicit usings enabled (file-scoped namespaces and global usings preferred).
      * Warnings treated as errors so the Release "warn as error" build (Gate 1)
        reports zero errors and zero warnings, EXCEPT CS8618.

    CS8618 ("Non-nullable field/property must contain a non-null value when
    exiting constructor") is exempted via WarningsNotAsErrors, NOT NoWarn, so it
    remains a warning rather than being escalated to an error or fully suppressed.
    This matches the Gate 1 phrasing "zero errors and zero warnings (excluding
    CS8618 nullable warnings)" and lets POCO entities and DTOs declare
    non-nullable reference properties (for example "public string PortalName
    { get; set; }") without breaking the build. The CLI warn-as-error flag sets
    TreatWarningsAsErrors=true globally but does not override WarningsNotAsErrors,
    so the CS8618 exemption still holds.

    This is the top-most Directory.Build.props for the backend tree: there is no
    Directory.Build.props at the repository root, and MSBuild stops at the first
    one it finds when walking up from each project. Therefore no parent import is
    declared here. Package references and SDK/OutputType selection are per-project
    concerns and are intentionally absent from this shared file.
    ============================================================================
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>12.0</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>CS8618</WarningsNotAsErrors>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
